---
/**
 * Where a seller connects his OWN clearing account — the screen the SaaS shape turns on.
 *
 * ── What this is NOT ──
 * It is not a form we send anywhere. Under the split model the seller handed us ten facts about his
 * business and we opened a merchant account FOR him (`ClearingDetailsForm.astro`); under this shape
 * he already has an account at his own provider, the buyer's money goes straight into it, and we
 * never hold a shekel of it. So the whole screen is "paste what your provider gave you", and the
 * strings are written to a person reading them with that provider's admin open in another tab —
 * every label is what HE is looking for over there, not what we would have called it
 * (`clearing-providers.ts` carries the same rule for the field labels themselves).
 *
 * ── Why the provider is buttons and not a dropdown ──
 * Native `<select>` is banned site-wide, and the list is short enough that opening something to
 * discover it holds five things is worse than showing five things. Same treatment the gender pair
 * in `ClearingDetailsForm` uses — `btn--accent` for the chosen one — so the two choosers on this
 * screen say "picked" the same way.
 *
 * ── The providers we cannot talk to yet are NOT shown at all (owner, 2026-09-08) ──
 * They were rendered disabled with a sentence explaining why. He read the screen and said the
 * quiet part: *"זה לא צריך להיות משהו שהיוזר בכלל רואה"*. He is right — a greyed-out row with an
 * apology beside it is our roadmap on a seller's settings screen, and it makes a list of six read
 * as a list of six choices, one of which is broken. A seller whose processor is missing learns
 * that from the list itself.
 * The registry still HOLDS them (`clearing-providers.ts`), the route still refuses them by id, and
 * `connectableProviders()` is what this list is built from — so an entry becomes visible the day
 * its fields are read from the vendor, and not before.
 *
 * ── What is on file is a HINT, never a value ──
 * A secret comes back from the server as four characters (`secret-box.ts#secretHint`), and the
 * input for it is left EMPTY with "leave blank to keep it unchanged" underneath. That is why
 * `saveSellerClearing` merges rather than replaces: an untouched secret arrives empty from the
 * browser, and a replace would wipe the key he did not retype every time he corrected a terminal
 * number.
 *
 * ── What this screen deliberately does NOT claim ──
 * It never says the shop can now take payment. `canTakePayments` also requires a successful
 * connection check against the provider, and that check does not exist yet (one adapter per
 * provider; GO_LIVE §3.1). Reporting "fields on file" is the honest half, and a card that promised
 * selling would be the promise a buyer discovers is false.
 */
import type { ClearingProvider } from '../../lib/clearing-providers.js';
import type { getT } from '../../i18n/index.js';

interface Props {
  /** Verified providers, in registry order — what a seller may actually pick today. */
  providers: ClearingProvider[];
  /** The provider he is on, or null when he has never connected one. */
  currentId: string | null;
  /** Per field name: is it set, and the hint to show beside it. Never a secret's value. */
  onFile: Record<string, { set: boolean; hint: string }>;
  /** Field names still empty on the CURRENT provider. */
  missing: string[];
  d: ReturnType<typeof getT>['dashboard'];
}

const { providers, currentId, onFile, missing, d } = Astro.props;

const current = providers.find((p) => p.id === currentId) ?? null;
/** Connected AND nothing left to paste — the closed summary state, same shape the bank block uses. */
const settled = !!current && missing.length === 0;
const missingLine = missing.length === 1 ? d.ownClearingMissingOne : d.ownClearingMissing.replace('{n}', String(missing.length));
---

<section class="card card--flat p-4 md:p-5 mb-4" id="own-clearing">
  <h3 class="text-[1.05rem] font-bold m-0">{d.ownClearingTitle}</h3>
  {/* The instruction, only while there is something to do. Left standing over the closed summary it
      told a seller who had already connected an account to go and connect one — prose above a screen
      that argues with the screen (`feedback_no_standing_screen_prose`). Seen on the real card, not
      reasoned about: the settled state was screenshotted with the sentence still on it. */}
  {!settled && <p class="muted m-0 mt-1 text-[0.82rem]">{d.ownClearingLead}</p>}

  {/* ── The closed summary ──
      Both halves are SERVER-rendered with `hidden` on the one that does not apply, never revealed by
      a script on load: a JS-gated visibility is the flash class this project already has a memory
      for (`project_injected_overlay_flash`). The server knows which state this is. */}
  <div
    id="own-clearing-summary"
    class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 flex-wrap mt-3 p-3 border [border-color:var(--color-border)] rounded-[var(--radius)]"
    hidden={!settled}
  >
    <p class="m-0 text-[0.9rem] font-semibold" id="own-clearing-summary-line">
      {current ? d.ownClearingOnFile.replace('{name}', current.name) : ''}
    </p>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 shrink-0">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" id="own-clearing-edit">{d.ownClearingEdit}</button>
      {/* Danger-red by default in `ConfirmModal`, which is right: this deletes what he pasted. */}
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" id="own-clearing-disconnect">{d.ownClearingDisconnect}</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <form id="own-clearing-form" hidden={settled} data-unsaved-guard>
    {/* The value lives in a real hidden INPUT so `FormData` carries it like every other field, and
        so the unsaved-changes bar can be told it moved through `announceValueChange` — the one
        sanctioned way to say so (guarded by `tests/unsaved-notice.test.ts`). */}
    <input type="hidden" name="provider" id="own-clearing-provider" value={currentId ?? ''} />

    <fieldset class="border-0 p-0 m-0 mt-4">
      <legend class="text-[0.85rem] mb-1.5 p-0">{d.ownClearingPick}</legend>

      {/* ── Which one is chosen, said in words (owner, 2026-09-08) ──
          A filled pill among six is a state a reader has to FIND before he can read it, and the one
          state that matters most — none chosen — has no filled pill to find at all. So the choice
          is stated on its own row above the pills, and the button beside it is what undoes it.
          `aria-live`: the row is rewritten under a press, and the press moves nothing else a screen
          reader would announce. */}
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap mb-2 text-[0.84rem]" aria-live="polite">
        <span id="own-clearing-state" class:list={['font-semibold', current ? '' : '[color:var(--color-muted)]']}>
          {current ? d.ownClearingChosen.replace('{name}', current.name) : d.ownClearingNone}
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex gap-2 flex-wrap" id="own-clearing-pick">
        {providers.map((p) => (
          <button
            type="button"
            class:list={['btn btn--sm', p.id === currentId ? 'btn--accent' : 'btn--ghost']}
            data-provider={p.id}
            aria-pressed={p.id === currentId}
          >{p.name}</button>
        ))}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    {/* One fieldset per provider, all server-rendered, all but the chosen one `hidden`. Rendering
        only the chosen one would mean a round trip on every press of a button whose whole job is to
        show the seller what he is about to be asked for. */}
    {providers.map((p) => (
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2" data-provider-fields={p.id} hidden={p.id !== currentId}>
        {p.fields.map((f) => (
          <label class="field">
            <span class="text-[0.85rem]">{f.label}</span>
            {/* `dir="ltr"`: every one of these values is ASCII, and ASCII on an RTL page groups the
                wrong way round when left to inherit. Same rule the bank fields follow.
                A secret renders EMPTY with its hint underneath — see the header. */}
            <input
              class="input"
              name={f.name}
              dir="ltr"
              autocomplete="off"
              maxlength="200"
              type={f.secret ? 'password' : 'text'}
              value={f.secret ? '' : (onFile[f.name]?.hint ?? '')}
            />
            <p class="muted m-0 mt-1 text-[0.76rem]">
              {f.help}
              {f.secret && onFile[f.name]?.set && (
                <> · <code dir="ltr">{onFile[f.name]!.hint}</code> {d.ownClearingSecretOnFile} · {d.ownClearingSecretKeep}</>
              )}
            </p>
          </label>
        ))}
      </div>
    ))}

    <p class="m-0 mt-3 text-[0.82rem]" id="own-clearing-missing" hidden={!current || missing.length === 0}>{missingLine}</p>
    <p class="hidden text-sm [color:var(--color-danger)] mt-1 mb-3" id="own-clearing-error" role="alert"></p>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-3">
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn--sm" id="own-clearing-save">{d.ownClearingSave}</button>
      {/* Beside Save, not up by the pills (owner, 2026-09-08). Undoing a choice is an ACTION, and
          the actions of this form are on its action row — a control living next to the thing it
          talks about is the arrangement everywhere else, and this was the exception. Clearing is a
          local undo (nothing is stored until he saves), so it is a ghost button; disconnecting an
          account that IS stored is destructive and lives on the closed summary behind a
          confirmation. */}
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" id="own-clearing-clear" hidden={!currentId}>{d.ownClearingClear}</button>
      {/* Present always, hidden until there is something to go back to — cancelling with nothing
          saved would close the fields over an empty summary card. Same reasoning as the bank
          block's cancel. */}
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" id="own-clearing-cancel" hidden={!settled}>{d.ownClearingCancel}</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</section>
